#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:1
#: 7efb0d2b51e9407d9cd2cdd07b75dcb3
msgid "How the pp calculation works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:3
#: cfec43a02e3d409a9a8e7b1c98c2f40b
msgid "`parsecore.Performance` is a pure-Python port of the **official osu! difficulty and performance algorithms** (ppy/osu, deploy `2026.702.1`) not of a third-party reimplementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:7
#: b60733c246354d6e8dabb8cc5bfae245
msgid "The pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:10
#: 84bab881222841c2858988a3f5999480
msgid "**Parse** the ``.osu`` file is decoded into hit objects and timing/difficulty/effect points with osu!-faithful float semantics (positions and curve math run in 32-bit floats, exactly like the game client)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:13
#: 8f64c1bb6bee49388d9827b212cc01a3
msgid "**Convert** if the target ruleset differs from the map's native mode, the map is converted first (taiko drum-roll splitting with scroll-speed effect points, catch mode flag, mania legacy pattern generator with osu!stable RNG)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:16
#: d9689503a01746d1975c19a3a7e0601a
msgid "**Preprocess** per-ruleset difficulty objects are built (distances, angles, rhythm groupings, effective BPM, ...)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:18
#: 5e8eaa8e69fa442c8e9eb342392bb909
msgid "**Skills** each ruleset evaluates its skills and aggregates them into the star rating:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:21
#: ed3abc49bb984ec5ac89dc8d7602f4bd
msgid "osu!: Aim (snap/flow), Speed, Reading, Flashlight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:22
#: 2b7038daf3104b049c78b37f5ecf1640
msgid "taiko: Rhythm, Reading, Colour, Stamina"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:23
#: 62d0da90f9bc4679990e5011cf47eac5
msgid "catch: Movement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:24
#: 39f9a1baa2574c4b92596bf2d085fa93
msgid "mania: Strain (individual + overall)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:26
#: 463ab33b47804a189085c9df5a69d0a0
msgid "**Performance** the score state (given explicitly or generated from accuracy and miss count) is combined with the difficulty attributes into pp, including miss penalties, slider-break estimation, and the classic/lazer scoring differences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:31
#: 8cba8dbddb894616b100ddb0e2c0149e
msgid "What's new in the 2026 Q2 rework"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:33
#: fdd9808a34754f0b8647d74f6638fe7d
msgid "parsecore implements the July 2026 rework: the AR/HD bonuses were replaced by a dedicated **Reading** skill, aim was split into **Snap** and **Flow** components, speed pp became **deviation-based**, taiko rhythm gained a long-gap penalty, and catch received a linear-spacing nerf."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/how-pp-works.md:38
#: e8f50a84b886409d9774865ced3c245b
msgid "Every step reproduces the C# reference **including its floating-point quirks**, which is what makes the results {doc}`bit-exact <bit-exactness>` rather than merely close."
msgstr ""

